{
  "version": "2.21",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "y2xNdf",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Uso",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "X8ZiJF",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Uso — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "O572gY",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "PURPOSE\nThe instance's usage record (ADR-032): the events the issues' usage metrics need, and the funnels from a call to action to the action it led to, read on one screen. Kept so a feature is kept, changed or deleted on what was done, not on what is remembered.\n\nENTRY POINTS\nAjustes hub → Uso (always listed: the day counters count even with the switch off). The switch, Registro de uso, lives in Estado y mantenimiento with the other instance switches. Back returns to Ajustes.\n\nSCREENS (LEFT → RIGHT)\nUso · Apagado (never turned on: the notice once, no funnels or capture, dashes in the table, the day counters) · Uso · Con datos.\n\nBUSINESS RULES\n• The switch gates event capture, not only this screen; it is off by default (ADR-032 §1). The day counters (Aperturas: per screen over 14 days, Panorama per day, the ? helps, Descubrir's weeks for D31) are always on, count nothing but opens, and live only here (D174).\n• Only catalogued events are recorded, each naming the question it answers (§2). No IP, user agent, session or free text (§3).\n• A funnel sets the offers of a week against the actions that came from them in that week (§4, §6). Each card leads with this week's counts, then the measured weeks' total; a percentage only past five offers, and never when an action outran its offers. An action whose offer was the week before reads as \"tomada esta semana, de una oferta anterior\".\n• Weeks read newest first, the current one headed Esta, so on a phone the cut-off columns are the oldest. A week counts as measured if the switch was on for any of it, known from the switch's last flip; an unmeasured week reads —, never 0, and the Total column sums the measured ones. With the switch on, \"Encendido desde …\" says where measuring starts.\n• Rows are kept 90 days. Opening this screen is counted: unread for 30 days with the switch on, the record is deleted (§9).\n\nCOPY SOURCE\nconfig/locales/es-MX.yml — admin.usage.show.*, admin.settings.show.uso*, settings.show.uso*. Event names: Usage::Domain::Catalogue; the question under each, admin.usage.show.preguntas.\n\nSTATES NOT DRAWN\n• Switch on and nothing recorded yet: the Con datos layout with every funnel and the capture reading \"Todavía no hay datos.\", and zeros in the table.\n• A funnel offered nothing this week: \"No se ofreció esta semana.\"\n• Switched off after recording: funnels and capture stay, weeks after the flip read —.\n• Ajustes hub: the Uso row carries an \"Apagado\" badge while the switch is off.\n• Any screen on desktop: the same column inside the SidebarNav shell.\n\nOPEN FINDINGS\nNone.\n\nHISTORY\n→ Log · Uso",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
